ve it  i do too david in october you know i  spoke with uh the directors matt and  tyler about the science of fear so i  have to ask and gail kind of alluded to  it you said that you love scary movies  you love the gore but what is your  favorite scary movie um they asked that  in the movie oh man  i always liked the shining because jack  nicholson's performance was so great in  that but there's so many great movies  coming out get out was incredible  hereditary's incredible midsomar like  there's just wild films coming out  you also have another side david in  addition to scary you like being a clown  you bought the rights to bozo he's in  clown school and you're in clown school  that just did not  is that you is that david  that's one of the older  okay  what is what is your appeal to cleveland  wgn  yeah what's your appeal with i love club  i was surprised to hear that i felt  i fell in love with clowns when i was a  kid in chicago watching bozo and he was  just  just i don't know it's joy and laughter  and i really want to bring that back to  the world i'm working with an  organization called healthy humor that  uh do medical clowning in in 15  hospitals throughout the country so i'm  going to study with them in february and  it's just about you know bringing some  light to the world  that's awesome well listen  you weren't clowning around in this film  we're absolutely incredible david  arquette thank you for joining us you  can see scream in theaters nationwide  starting friday

